powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "source": "{% comment %}
  Radio group for one single-choice question. Include with:
  (% include 'OT Answer Options' response_type: 120910005 selected: 120910301 question: '<guid>' is_tax: false %)

  `is_tax` is the REVIEW's discipline, and 120910006 is the one scale that reads differently
  by it. Pass it on every include: an omitted one is falsy, which renders the scale's own
  wording - the safe half of the pair, and the one six AQS sections share.

  The permitted subset per response type is the AD-023 rule; it is mirrored here for
  rendering and enforced server-side by ResponseRules.PermittedChoices, which is the
  authority. A value added here without a matching change there is refused on save.

  Single select falls to the else branch and means Primary root cause only. Q-TAX-02
  was retyped to Pass / Fail / Insufficient evidence under AD-055 (its third option now reads
  "Pass with issues" in every Tax context; see below), which is what makes
  that unambiguous.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  Labels and order here are the document's INLINE ones, which are not always the grid's.
  Where the Checker Checklist draws an outcome scale beside its question rather than as a
  tick column it sets it in upper case - PASS / FAIL, YES / NO, PASS / PASS WITH ISSUES /
  ... - and it orders the tax check outcome PASS, PASS WITH ISSUES, FAIL. Primary root cause
  is title case on the document and stays as it is. The app makes the same reading in
  checklistForm.ts, inlineOptionsFor.

  120910006's third option is the one place two readings differ in WORDING and not only in
  case: on a TAX review 120910302 reads "PASS WITH ISSUES", and everywhere else it reads
  "INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE" as the suitability grid heads it (AD-055 amended). The rename sits
  here rather than on the scale because 120910006 is shared with S-E1 to S-E5 and S-CRP, and
  renaming the option itself would have relabelled six AQS sections nobody asked to change.

  Until 2026-09-19 that rename and that reorder were applied to EVERY 120910006 question
  this include drew, on the reading that only Q-TAX-02 was ever drawn inline at this scale.
  AD-123 checklist administration made that false. Retyping a question to this scale breaks
  its section's uniform grid, the section falls to this include, and an AQS question was
  drawn as a tax check: a checker ticking what read "PASS WITH ISSUES" saved 120910302,
  Insufficient evidence, which is a non-pass that raises remediation. The grid path above
  had always tested the discipline; this one now does too.

  Only the labels and their order move. The values are unchanged, and
  ResponseRules.PermittedChoices is still the authority on which of them may be saved.
{% endcomment %}
{% case response_type %}
  {% when 120910005 %}
    {% assign values = '120910300,120910301' | split: ',' %}
    {% assign labels = 'PASS,FAIL' | split: ',' %}
  {% when 120910006 %}
    {% if is_tax %}
      {% assign values = '120910300,120910302,120910301' | split: ',' %}
      {% assign labels = 'PASS,PASS WITH ISSUES,FAIL' | split: ',' %}
    {% else %}
      {% assign values = '120910300,120910301,120910302' | split: ',' %}
      {% assign labels = 'PASS,FAIL,INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE' | split: ',' %}
    {% endif %}
  {% when 120910007 %}
    {% assign values = '120910305,120910306' | split: ',' %}
    {% assign labels = 'YES,NO' | split: ',' %}
  {% when 120910008 %}
    {% assign values = '120910305,120910306,120910307' | split: ',' %}
    {% assign labels = 'YES,NO,N/A' | split: ',' %}
  {% when 120910009 %}
    {% assign values = '120910305,120910306,120910302' | split: ',' %}
    {% assign labels = 'YES,NO,INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE' | split: ',' %}
  {% when 120910010 %}
    {% assign values = '120910300,120910303,120910302,120910304' | split: ',' %}
    {% assign labels = 'PASS,PASS WITH ISSUES,INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE,POTENTIAL HARM' | split: ',' %}
  {% else %}
    {% comment %}
      Primary root cause. Reached only if something other than the review page includes this
      for that type: the review page draws it itself, as the document does, in a 3x3 table of
      its own rather than as a value cell of the block's table.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% assign values = '120910320,120910321,120910322,120910323,120910324,120910325,120910326,120910327,120910328' | split: ',' %}
    {% assign labels = 'FactFind quality,Risk / capacity mismatch,Research / rationale,Charges / value,Client communication,Process / documentation,AML / CRA,Retirement Proposition,Adviser judgement' | split: ',' %}
{% endcase %}

{% comment %}
  `locked` is an optional pipe-delimited list of values this question may not currently take,
  e.g. '|120910300|120910303|'. It is what item 10 (2026-09-19) uses to take PASS and PASS
  WITH ISSUES off the advice quality grade once a Suitability core check has been answered
  Insufficient evidence.

  Delimited rather than compared as a bare substring, the same way the multi-select above
  builds optkey: none of these values is a substring of another today, and a list that
  depends on that staying true is a list that breaks quietly.

  Rendering only. GradingRules.SuitabilityGradeRefusal is the authority and refuses the write
  itself, in ResponseGuardPlugin and again in the command that completes the review, so a
  value locked here and not there would still be saveable and a value locked there and not
  here is simply refused with a sentence.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  `question_text` names every radio for a screen reader (F54, fixed 2026-09-21), so each one
  announces "Tax check outcome: PASS" rather than a bare "PASS".

  It is on the INPUT and not on a wrapping group, deliberately. Power Pages injects
  `role="radiogroup"` onto the value cell and `role="group"` onto the row at RUNTIME - neither
  is in this solution's markup, and the server-rendered HTML carries neither - and it injects
  them with no accessible name. That `role="group"` also overrides the native row semantics a
  screen reader would otherwise have used to read the row header, so the fallback goes with
  it. Naming the group would mean fighting an attribute we do not emit and cannot see from
  here; naming each option cannot be undone by anything the platform adds afterwards.

  It is also the pattern this page already proved: the grid-layout branch of OT Review Detail
  has always emitted an sr-only `<label>` reading "{question}: {option}". This gives the
  non-grid branch the same guarantee by a route that works whether or not a label element is
  wanted in the layout.

  Optional, so any caller that does not pass it keeps exactly the markup it had.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="opts">
  {% for value in values %}
    {% assign valuekey = '|' | append: value | append: '|' %}
    {% assign is_locked = false %}
    {% if locked and locked contains valuekey %}{% assign is_locked = true %}{% endif %}
    <label class="opt{% if is_locked %} opt--locked{% endif %}"><input type="radio" class="cc-box"
             name="q-{{ question }}"
             value="{{ value }}"
             {% if question_text %}aria-label="{{ question_text | escape }}: {{ labels[forloop.index0] }}"{% endif %}
             data-ot-input{% if is_locked %} data-ot-lockable{% endif %}{% unless editable %} disabled{% endunless %}{% if is_locked %} disabled{% endif %}
             {% if selected and selected == value %}checked{% endif %} /> {{ labels[forloop.index0] }}</label>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
"
}
